(1) INFO ABOUT UTILITY
=======================================================================================================

`catpkg-make` is a build utility for the CatPackage project.

This utility provides builds related to CatPackage and allows you to assemble
the latest versions of catstrap, catpkg, and other components distributed
with the project.

It provides predefined build configurations for creating executable catstrap
archives, individual `.catpackage` packages, filesystem packages, and the
catpkg-make executable itself.

The target processor architecture can be selected during the build process
where supported.

At the moment, CatPackage is in beta testing. The build system and its
internal interfaces may change between versions, and catpkg-make therefore
cannot yet provide complete and stable documentation for all available
build operations.


(2) USAGE
=======================================================================================================

Run `catpkg-make` and select the required build from the interactive menu:

========================================
        CATPKG MAKE                     
The CATPKG utility builder.                                        
========================================           
Welcome to the CATPKG utility builder! Choose which build you need:
1) Building catstrap-catpkg-*-(aarch64/x86_64)
2) Building catstrap-catpkg-lite-*-(aarch64/x86_64)
3) Building catstrap-catpkg-net-*-(aarch64/x86_64)
4) Building catstrap-catpkg-custom-*-(aarch64/x86_64)
5) Building catstrap ( Empty )

6) Building the catpkg-(aarch64/x86_64)@*.catpackage
7) Building the catstraplib-(aarch64/x86_64)@*.catpackage
8) Building the catstrap-bin-(aarch64/x86_64)@*.catpackage
9) Building the catpkg-build-(aarch64/x86_64)@1.0.0b.catpackage

10) Building the filesystem@1.0.catpackage
11) Building the filesystem-android@1.0.catpackage

12) catpkg-make-(aarch64/x86_64) ( Update )
Enter a number: ^C


< P.S. About options >

1 - This option creates a package:

`.tmp/catpkg-(aarch64/x86_64)@X.X.X.catpackage`

The target processor architecture can be selected during the build.
The package version is automatically obtained from:

`build-data/PACKAGEINFO`

The resulting `.catpackage` file can then be used by other catpkg-make
build operations.


2 - This option creates the main executable catpkg installation file
with support for selecting the target processor architecture.

The package produced by:

`Building the catpkg-(aarch64/x86_64)@X.X.X.catpackage`

is used as part of this build process.


3 - This option updates an existing build master or creates a new one,
with support for selecting the target processor architecture.


-> To confirm, press “Enter”.

Regardless of the selected option, enter the required number at:

`Enter a number:`

If the selected build supports multiple processor architectures,
catpkg-make will then display the architectures available for that build.

Select the required architecture:

`aarch64`
    64-bit ARM architecture.

`x86_64`
    64-bit x86 architecture.


-> To confirm, press “Enter”.

After confirmation, catpkg-make prepares the required build environment
and starts the selected assembly process.

Depending on the selected option, the build process may create a
`.catpackage` package, an executable catstrap archive, or another
CatPackage project component.

Generated package names generally contain the package name, target
architecture where applicable, and package version.

Example:

`catpkg-x86_64@*.catpackage`

The exact output and intermediate files depend on the selected build
configuration.


